! WP-PF.1 family deck: the IEC-868 `Pstcalc` executive command (Pascal
! `ExecHelper.DoPstCalc` over `Shared/Pstcalc.pas`). A trivial 3-phase circuit
! is solved, then one `Pstcalc` runs the flicker Pst calculator over a 700-point
! modulated-sine RMS array (dt=1 s, freq=60, 120 V lamp) -> one 10-minute Pst
! value in GlobalResult. The command runs live on both engines at compile time
! (a `not_ported`/parse/panic regression fails the family gate's post-compile
! no-error assert). The byte-exact Pst-value comparison across the full
! npts/shape/lamp/freq/dt matrix is the golden `golden_pstcalc.rs`; the harness
! captures GlobalResult only AFTER its own solve (which clears the Pstcalc
! result), so this deck's compare_global_result compares the post-solve strings.
